// The Automatics fire-rate bands (skillperks 09). A gun's band is part of the gun (owner, 2026-11-27): its base tics
// between shots in the way it is firing, without mods, perks or other fire-rate bonuses, at full speed for a gun that
// spins up. 4 or more tics is the slow band, 3 the middle band, 1-2 the fast band. Stock Doom's Chaingun fires every 4
// tics. DRLA's guns come from a table read from DRLA's own DECORATE by tools/automatics/derive_bands.py (--check fails
// if it is stale or a listed gun has no rate). A gun has a row per way it fires: per firing mode (the count of a mode
// item its AltFire switches, such as the Grammaton Beretta's semi, burst and full auto) and for an alternate fire that
// shoots (used while the gun's bAltFire is set). Classes are names only, so the table does nothing without DRLA. A gun
// on neither list has no band.
class DoomerfallAutomaticBands abstract
{
	enum EBand { BandNone, BandSlow, BandMiddle, BandFast }

	clearscope static int BandFromTics(int t)
	{
		if (t <= 0) return BandNone;
		if (t >= 4) return BandSlow;
		return t == 3 ? BandMiddle : BandFast;
	}

	// The band of a gun as it fires now: its mode (the holder's mode item count) and primary or alternate fire.
	clearscope static int BandOf(Weapon w)
	{
		return w ? BandFromTics(TicsOf(w.GetClass(), w.Owner, w.bAltFire)) : BandNone;
	}

	// The band of a gun the player fired: the instance they carry, else the class's primary fire.
	clearscope static int BandOfGun(Actor holder, class<Weapon> gun)
	{
		let w = holder && gun ? Weapon(holder.FindInventory(gun)) : null;
		return w ? BandOf(w) : BandFromTics(TicsOf(gun, null, false));
	}

	// The base tics between shots of a gun class: its own rows, else its nearest listed parent's. Among a class's rows,
	// the one for this fire (alternate rows only while alt firing, else primary) whose mode count the holder has.
	// 0 when unknown.
	clearscope static int TicsOf(class<Actor> c, Actor holder, bool alt)
	{
